course: dictionary
lesson: 16154
title: Witchcraft and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Witchcraft is the use of magic powers, especially spells and potions, as in stories. «The witch used witchcraft to turn the prince into a frog.» The witch and the spell tell you the word is about magic.
explain: Long ago, some innocent people were wrongly accused of witchcraft, which was treated as a crime. «The villagers wrongly accused the old woman of witchcraft.» The word wrongly is the clue: she did not do it, and the charge was false.
explain: People also use witchcraft as a joke when something is so clever or surprising that it seems like magic. «Dad fixed the laptop in two minutes. "That's pure witchcraft!" said Mia.» Mia does not mean real magic here; she means the fix was amazing.
fact: Witchcraft is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say some witchcraft, not a witchcraft.
fact: «Witchcraft» means the use of magic powers, especially to do harm, as in fairy tales and fantasy books.
fact: In history, «witchcraft» was a crime that innocent people were wrongly accused of, such as in the witch trials in Europe and in Salem, Massachusetts, in 1692.
fact: Informally, «witchcraft» can mean something so clever or surprising it seems like magic.
fact: Some people today follow Wicca, a modern religion that they also call witchcraft or the Craft.
exercise: «The witch used witchcraft to turn the prince into a frog.» What is witchcraft in this sentence? | A type of animal | A long journey on a broomstick | *The use of magic powers | A kind of cooking with herbs
exercise: «The villagers wrongly accused the old woman of witchcraft.» What does wrongly accused mean? | *Blamed for a crime she did not do | Thanked for a kind deed | Given a reward for her cooking | Chosen to be the village leader
exercise: «Dad fixed the laptop in two minutes. "That's pure witchcraft!" said Mia.» What does Mia mean? | Dad was very angry with the laptop | Dad had really cast a spell on the laptop | *Dad's fix was so clever it seemed like magic | The laptop was made of wood
test: What kind of word is witchcraft? | A verb, meaning to cast a spell | An adjective, meaning magical | *A noun, a thing or an idea | A number
test: Which word is closest in meaning to witchcraft in the sense of magic powers? | Kindness | Sleep | Cooking | *Magic
exam: In «Many innocent people were accused of witchcraft in the past», what does witchcraft mean? | A festival with music and dancing | A kind of medicine for colds | *A crime people were wrongly accused of | A sport played on ice
